Unchanged-macroblock hints for OpenH264 v2.7.0 (DevBox-Gateway-kvm).

SSourcePicture gains pUnchangedMacroblocks/iUnchangedMacroblockCount: one
byte per 16x16 macroblock, nonzero certifying that its Y/U/V source samples
equal the previous successfully encoded picture's. Ports the pure-Go
encoder's hint handling (pkg/h264/internal/encoder) so both produce the same
bitstream:
  - forced zero-MV P_SKIP for certified macroblocks whose collocated
    reference macroblock was a zero-MV P_SKIP (unchanged.cpp);
  - reconstruction reuse for those macroblocks;
  - VAA SADs that skip certified macroblocks (vaacalculation.cpp);
  - source copies limited to the damage since each buffer's last refresh
    (wels_preprocess_unchanged.cpp);
  - runs of such macroblocks coded without per-macroblock mode decision
    bookkeeping, and multi-slice pictures with few other macroblocks coded
    on the calling thread instead of the thread pool.
Pictures without hints encode exactly as upstream.

